# Hono Guidelines

Core guidelines for building type-safe, maintainable APIs using Hono. These patterns ensure consistent, secure, and performant backend services.

## Core Principles
- **KISS (Keep It Simple, Stupid)** - Always choose the simplest, most maintainable solution
- **TypeScript First** - Always use TypeScript with strict typing everywhere
- **Less is More** - Always avoid unnecessary complexity, the best code is no code
- **Business Logic in lib/** - Always separate concerns cleanly

## Route Organization
- Always structure routes using dot notation: `v1.auth.shopify/`, `v1.users/`
- Always keep three files per route: `schema.ts`, `index.ts`, `lib/`
- Always organize business logic functions in separate files within `lib/`

✅ Good:
```typescript
// Clear route structure
src/app/routes/
├── v1.users/              # Maps to /v1/users/*
│   ├── schema.ts          # Route schemas & types
│   ├── index.ts           # Route handlers
│   └── lib/               # Business logic
│       ├── index.ts       # Exports
│       ├── create-user.ts
│       └── get-user.ts
```

❌ Bad:
```typescript
// Wrong: Nested or inconsistent structure
src/routes/
├── v1/                    # Wrong: Nested version
│   └── users/             # Wrong: Nested resource
│       └── users.ts       # Wrong: Single file for all routes
```

## Schema Definition
- Always use Zod with `DTO` suffix for API contracts
- Always include OpenAPI examples for all fields
- Always use descriptive parameter names (`userId`, not `id`)
- Always export TypeScript types from schemas

✅ Good:
```typescript
// schema.ts
import { createRoute, z } from '@hono/zod-openapi';
import { JsonSuccessResponse, BadRequestResponse } from '@repo/hono-utils';

const SUserDto = z
  .object({
    id: z.string().uuid().openapi({ example: '123e4567-e89b-12d3' }),
    email: z.string().email().openapi({ example: 'user@example.com' }),
    name: z.string().openapi({ example: 'John Doe' })
  })
  .openapi('UserDto');

export type TUserDto = z.infer<typeof SUserDto>;

export const CreateUserRoute = createRoute({
  method: 'post',
  path: '/v1/users',
  tags: ['users'],
  summary: 'Create user',
  operationId: 'createUser',
  request: {
    body: {
      content: {
        'application/json': {
          schema: SUserDto.omit({ id: true })
        }
      }
    }
  },
  responses: {
    201: JsonSuccessResponse(SUserDto),
    400: BadRequestResponse
  }
});
```

❌ Bad:
```typescript
// Wrong: Missing DTO suffix, no examples, generic parameters
const SUser = z.object({        // Wrong: Missing Dto suffix
  email: z.string(),            // Wrong: No OpenAPI example
  name: z.string()
});

export const CreateRoute = createRoute({
  path: '/users/{id}',          // Wrong: Generic 'id' parameter
  responses: {
    200: { description: 'OK' }  // Wrong: No typed response
  }
});
```

## Route Implementation
- Always keep route handlers clean and focused on HTTP concerns
- Always import business logic functions from `./lib`
- Always use consistent error handling with `AppError`
- Always validate inputs with `c.req.valid()`

✅ Good:
```typescript
// index.ts
import { AppError } from '@repo/hono-utils';
import { router } from '@/app/router';
import { createUser, getUser } from './lib';
import { CreateUserRoute, GetUserRoute } from './schema';

router.openapi(CreateUserRoute, async (c) => {
  const input = c.req.valid('json');
  const user = await createUser(input);
  return c.json(user, 201);
});

router.openapi(GetUserRoute, async (c) => {
  const { userId } = c.req.valid('param');
  const user = await getUser(userId);
  return c.json(user, 200);
});
```

❌ Bad:
```typescript
// Wrong: Business logic mixed with HTTP concerns
router.post('/users', async (c) => {
  const data = await c.req.json();     // Wrong: No validation
  
  // Wrong: Database operations in route handler
  const existing = await db.user.findUnique({ 
    where: { email: data.email } 
  });
  
  if (existing) {
    return c.json({ error: 'User exists' }, 409); // Wrong: Custom error format
  }
  
  const user = await db.user.create({ data }); // Wrong: No error handling
  return c.json(user);
});
```

## Business Logic Organization
- Always separate each operation into its own file
- Always export all functions from `lib/index.ts`
- Always use proper TypeScript types for inputs and outputs
- Always handle errors with `AppError`

✅ Good:
```typescript
// lib/index.ts
export * from './create-user';
export * from './get-user';

// lib/create-user.ts
import { AppError } from '@repo/hono-utils';
import { db } from '@/lib/db';
import type { TCreateUserDto, TUserDto } from '../schema';

export async function createUser(input: TCreateUserDto): Promise<TUserDto> {
  const existing = await db.user.findUnique({
    where: { email: input.email }
  });
  
  if (existing != null) {
    throw new AppError('#ERR_USER_EXISTS', 409, {
      detail: 'User already exists'
    });
  }
  
  const user = await db.user.create({ data: input });
  return user;
}
```

❌ Bad:
```typescript
// Wrong: All operations in one file, no types
// lib/operations.ts
export async function createUser(data) {        // Wrong: No types
  return db.user.create({ data });              // Wrong: No validation
}

export async function getUser(id) {
  const user = await db.user.findUnique({ where: { id } });
  if (!user) throw new Error('Not found');      // Wrong: Generic error
  return user;
}
```

## Error Handling
- Always use `AppError` from `@repo/hono-utils`
- Always include error codes with `#ERR_` prefix
- Always provide helpful detail messages
- Always re-throw `AppError` instances in route handlers

✅ Good:
```typescript
// In business logic
if (user == null) {
  throw new AppError('#ERR_USER_NOT_FOUND', 404, {
    detail: 'User not found'
  });
}
```

❌ Bad:
```typescript
// Wrong: Generic error handling
if (!user) {
  throw new Error('User not found');           // Wrong: Generic Error
}

// Wrong: Custom error responses
try {
  const user = await getUser(id);
  return c.json(user);
} catch (e) {
  return c.json({ error: e.message }, 500);      // Wrong: Custom format
}
```

